hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2954","**\nNarrated to us Al-Rabee’, narrated to us Bishr ibn Bakr, on the authority of Al-Awzaa’ee, who said: Muhammad ibn Ibraaheem ibn Al-Haarith Al-Taymee narrated to me, who said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, who said: ‘Aa’ishah (RA) narrated to me, who said:\n\n*The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Ifaadh (the Farewell Tawaaf), then he wanted from Safiyyah what a man wants from his wife. It was said to him, \She is menstruating.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Is she going to detain us?\"" They said"," \""She has already performed the Ifaadh.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took her away with him.*"""
